## Pipeline Overview

The scraper (`lament-scrapper`) is an automated CLI worker that populates the Lament media catalog. It integrates multiple APIs and command-line utilities:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Input["Track Query Input (URL / Track Name)"] --> Step1["1. Metadata Lookup (Spotify / Last.fm / Deezer / iTunes)"]
    Step1 --> Step2["2. Audio Search & Extraction (yt-dlp raw Opus/AAC rip)"]
    Step2 --> Step3["3. HLS Packaging (FFmpeg segmenting .m3u8 + .ts)"]
    Step3 --> Step4["4. Visual Asset Enrichment (Last.fm & Deezer via sharp WebP)"]
    Step4 --> Step5["5. Lyrics Fetching (Genius / LRC synced text)"]
    Step5 --> Step6["6. Storage & Database Insertion (R2 Upload & Turso Record Creation)"]
```

---

## Anti-Duplication Controls

To prevent duplicate track records:

- Every track row stores an `original_id` field (e.g. `yt_d9f8a2b` or Spotify ID) enforced with a `UNIQUE` SQL index constraint.
- The scraper queries `tracks WHERE original_id = ?` prior to audio downloading to skip existing songs.
